The widget DOES call `widget.service.applyModelWindowOverride(provider, modelId)` after the write seam. So the live apply should rebuild. Why didn't `agentModel.contextWindow` change to 131072?

`applyModelWindowOverride(provider, modelId)` reinstalls the global from `layer ?? _capabilityOverrides ?? loadAppCapabilityOverrides()`. In the TEST, `modelCapabilityOverrides` (process-wide global) is null at setUp; the write seam only updates the local `pinned` variable — it does NOT write to any real store. So `applyModelWindowOverride` reloads `loadAppCapabilityOverrides()` from the USER CONFIG — which is the test sandbox (no overrides persisted — write seam is a fake!). Result: the override layer reinstalls EMPTY → rebuild resolves the chain without the pin → contextWindow stays 1048576.

In MY earlier in-session version, the same seam existed and the test PASED... because my in-session test's write seam ALSO set `modelCapabilityOverrides` global (I saw that code in the earlier round: `modelCapabilityOverrides = value == null ? ModelCapabilityOverrides() : (..set(...))`). The committed test dropped that, relying on... maybe the committed AgentService behavior differs (e.g., applyModelWindowOverride uses the write-seam result?). The prior round's committed test presumably passed in their runs — or maybe they never ran it green (the round was cut off mid-verification — the transcript shows the compile error unresolved at restart).

Regardless: the committed TEST as-is fails. Fix: make the write seam ALSO install the process-wide override (the real write path does exactly that on next boot; the seam must simulate the persisted state), i.e.:

```dart
write: (provider, modelId, value) async {
 writes.add((provider, modelId, value));
 pinned = value;
 modelCapabilityOverrides = value == null
     ? ModelCapabilityOverrides()
     : (ModelCapabilityOverrides()
       ..set(provider, modelId, ModelCapabilityOverride(contextWindow: value)));
 return '/home/.fah/config.yaml';
},
``

That mirrors the real persistence the fake replaces. Check ModelCapabilityOverrides API (from T4 test file: `ModelCapabilityOverrides()..set('ain','big',ModelCapabilityOverride(contextWindow: value))` — that shape appeared in the earlier transcript, verify quickly in the SDK.

